# =============================================================================
# ai-eval-lab - credentials template
# =============================================================================
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#
#   1. Copy it:      cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. Edit .env.local and paste your real keys into the empty values.
#   3. Never commit .env.local. It is gitignored. This file is the only
#      credential-shaped file that is tracked, and it holds no values.
#
# The harness reads .env.local automatically (python-dotenv). If you export the
# variables in your shell instead, that works too - the .env.local values are
# just the default.
#
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. A key pasted into a commit, a chat, or a handoff file
# is a leaked key. If that happens, rotate it, then write it down.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MINIMUM TO START
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# You need exactly ONE model provider key to run the first sessions. Put it in
# .env.local and leave the rest empty:
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=...        <- recommended, free tier, no card
#   or GROQ_API_KEY=...
#   or OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
#   or run Ollama locally and set nothing at all
#
# Everything else below is optional and can be filled in later, in the order
# the sessions need it.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEY MAP
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   KEY                        WHAT IT DOES                      NEEDED BY
#   ------------------------   ------------------------------   -----------
#   GEMINI_API_KEY             default generator AND judge       S-002
#   GROQ_API_KEY               fallback generator / judge        S-002
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY         fallback generator / judge        S-002
#   LANGSMITH_API_KEY          tracing + datasets + experiments  S-001
#   (Phoenix / Langfuse)       local, no key, no account         S-004
#
# WHY THE JUDGE CAN USE A DIFFERENT KEY THAN THE GENERATOR
#
# A model that judges its own output scores it more generously - that is
# self-preference bias, and it inflates every score you report. Being able
# to point the judge at a different provider is the cheapest defense there
# is, and it is why the provider access is an interface rather than a
# direct SDK call. Set GEMINI for generation and GROQ (or OpenRouter) for
# judging, and say so in your write-up.
#
# =============================================================================


# --- PROVIDERS: generator and judge -----------------------------------------
# Only one is required to start. All are OpenAI- or Gemini-compatible; the
# harness picks whichever has a key.

# PRIMARY - Gemini free tier. No card required.
#   Get a key:  https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Free tier:  https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/rate-limits
#   Pricing:    https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing
#   Confirm which model is currently free-tier before you rely on it; the
#   lineup moves. gemini-2.5-flash is the conservative default.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# FALLBACK 1 - Groq. Fast, generous free tier, OpenAI-compatible.
#   Get a key:  https://console.groq.com/keys
#   Models:     https://console.groq.com/docs/models
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# FALLBACK 2 - OpenRouter. Many free models, one OpenAI-compatible base URL.
#   Get a key:  https://openrouter.ai/keys
#   Free models: https://openrouter.ai/models?max_price=0
#   Leave OPENROUTER_MODEL empty to use the provider default.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# FALLBACK 3 - Ollama. Fully local and offline. No key, no account, no cost.
#   Install:     https://ollama.com/download
#   Pull a model: ollama pull qwen2.5:7b
#   Then:        ollama serve
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b


# --- OBSERVABILITY ----------------------------------------------------------
# Traces are how a failing run becomes a test case. You will need one of
# these three by S-001.

# LangSmith - free Developer tier, 5k base traces/month then pay-as-you-go.
#   Sign up:    https://smith.langchain.com
#   API key:    https://smith.langchain.com/settings/tokens
#   Pricing:    https://www.langchain.com/pricing
#   C1's platform exercises need this - the course runs inside LangSmith.
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
LANGSMITH_TRACING=false

# Arize Phoenix - 100% free to self-host. No account, no key.
#   Start it:   phoenix serve
#   Docs:       https://arize.com/docs/phoenix/self-hosting
#   C2's five labs run against a local Phoenix, so this is the free path
#   through the most hands-on course in the program.
PHOENIX_ENABLED=false
PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:6006

# Langfuse - open source, free to self-host. Only if you run it.
#   Docs:       https://langfuse.com/self-hosting
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
LANGFUSE_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:3001
